The streaming chat needs a Stop button. `streamReply(prompt, signal)` streams into `reply` state and passes `signal` to `fetch`. The requirements are:

- Stop cancels the network request and keeps the text received so far;
- sending a new prompt cancels any previous stream;
- leaving the page cancels it too;
- a stopped reply must not show an error message.

Which implementation meets every requirement?

options.text:
```jsx
const controllerRef = useRef(null);
useEffect(() => () => controllerRef.current?.abort(), []);

async function send(prompt) {
  controllerRef.current?.abort();
  const controller = new AbortController();
  controllerRef.current = controller;
  try {
    await streamReply(prompt, controller.signal);
  } catch (err) {
    if (err.name !== 'AbortError') setError(err);
  }
}
const stop = () => controllerRef.current?.abort();
```

